      "problem": "A sphere has a diameter of $3 \\: \\textrm{in}.$ Find the surface area of the sphere.",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS =  4  \\pi r^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\dfrac{3}{2} \\: \\textrm{in}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS =  4  \\pi \\left(\\dfrac {3} {2} \\right)^2 = 9\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^2.\n$$",
